---
import Education from '../../layouts/Education.astro';
import TeachingDownloads from '../../components/TeachingDownloads.astro';
import {learningOutcomes,glossary,lessonCase,lessonAgenda,worksheet,workedAnswers,depthExamples} from '../../data/education-kit.mjs';
let elapsed=0;const timeline=lessonAgenda.map(entry=>{const start=elapsed;elapsed+=entry.minutes;return {...entry,range:`${start}–${elapsed}`};});
---
<Education title="What changed, and what happened anyway?" description="A ready-to-adapt 50-minute lesson on evidence, costs, counterfactuals and the people who can shape a decision." filePath="src/data/education-kit.mjs" active="teach">
  <a slot="actions" class="btn" href="#case">Read the fictional case</a><a slot="actions" class="btn btn-ghost" href="#worksheet">Use the worksheet</a>
  <section><h2>Prepare one session.</h2><p>No advance reading is needed. Print or share the case and worksheet, offer pens and an optional calculator, and put this map where everyone can use it: <strong>givers → signals → channels → work → outcomes</strong>. Leave room for feedback to change a decision.</p><p>Offer quiet reading, spoken or written responses, large print and the option to pass. Use assigned perspectives so no one needs to disclose a personal belief, financial situation or experience of receiving help. The proposed timing can be adapted by the educator.</p><h3>Intended learning outcomes</h3><ol>{learningOutcomes.map(outcome=><li>{outcome}</li>)}</ol><TeachingDownloads ids={['facilitator-guide','student-worksheet']} /></section>
  <section><h2>A proposed 50-minute agenda</h2><div class="education-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Lesson agenda, scroll horizontally if needed" tabindex="0"><table class="education-table"><caption>Proposed timings; no learning effect has been established</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Minutes</th><th scope="col">Facilitator action</th><th scope="col">Learner output</th></tr></thead><tbody>{timeline.map(entry=><tr><th scope="row">{entry.range} ({entry.minutes} min)</th><td>{entry.activity}</td><td>{entry.output}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
  <section id="case"><p class="eyebrow">Every detail is invented</p><h2>{lessonCase.title}</h2><p>{lessonCase.intro}</p><div class="education-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Fictional case figures, scroll horizontally if needed" tabindex="0"><table class="education-table"><caption>Fictional recorded values</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Record</th></tr></thead><tbody>{lessonCase.records.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.label}</th><td>{row.value}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><ul>{lessonCase.limitations.map(limit=><li>{limit}</li>)}</ul><div class="education-grid">{lessonCase.counterfactuals.map(card=><article class="education-card"><p class="eyebrow">Assumption · not evidence</p><h3>{card.label}</h3><p>{card.description}</p></article>)}</div><p class="education-limit">The case provides no basis for choosing either card as the correct comparison. Neither identifies the impact of a particular donor’s gift or a real charity.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Give the words a clear meaning.</h2><dl>{glossary.map(item=><><dt><strong>{item.term}</strong></dt><dd>{item.definition}</dd></>)}</dl></section>
  <section id="worksheet"><p class="eyebrow">Student worksheet</p><h2>Make the reasoning visible.</h2><p>Work alone or with a partner. Use words, a diagram or an explanation aloud. A learner can keep the sheet without adding a name or submitting anything online.</p>{worksheet.map(question=><article class="education-session" id={question.id.toLowerCase()}><p class="eyebrow">{question.id}</p><h3>{question.title}</h3><p>{question.prompt}</p>{question.steps?.length>0&&<ol>{question.steps.map(step=><li>{step}</li>)}</ol>}</article>)}</section>
  <section><h2>Depth describes where work acts.</h2><p>These are fictional activity descriptions. Each level may be needed; a higher number is not a better moral grade or proof of effectiveness. The six proposed sources—story, coordination, vision, attention, status and gatekeepers—remain hypotheses about the system.</p><div class="education-grid">{depthExamples.map(example=><article class="education-card"><p class="eyebrow">{example.level} · {example.name}</p><h3>{example.question}</h3><p>{example.example}</p></article>)}</div></section>
  <section id="answers"><p class="eyebrow">Facilitator notes · openly available</p><h2>Worked answers, with room to disagree.</h2><p>Check arithmetic and claim labels. Different decisions can be well reasoned when evidence, values and limits are clear. Classroom performance does not establish charitable impact, retained learning or professional competence.</p>{workedAnswers.map(answer=><details class="education-answer"><summary>{answer.id}: {answer.title}</summary>{answer.paragraphs.map(paragraph=><p>{paragraph}</p>)}</details>)}</section>
</Education>
